{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566645-roll-playing-totem-creation","id":566645,"title":"Roll playing totem creation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-24T10:27:04-07:00","id":566645,"title":"Roll playing totem creation","content":"I was going to start off our first session with the group binding it's totem, and establishing it's alpha. But I can't find anything in werewolf 2e that describes the spirit/totem binding process. Is there a gift or Rite necessary for binding your totem? Do you have to be in the hisil, if not, would it be easier in terms hisil? <br /> <br /> Do you have to hunt down the spirit and forcibly bind it as your totem, or do you negotiate with it? Is either route viable? <br /> <br /> How do you determine what sort of spirit it's going to be?<br /> <br /> .<br /> Mt idea, is for the pack to make their totem beforehand, and during my intro/prelude session, thet enter the hisil, and hunt down the kind of spirit they want to bind... just kind of lost on the binding part","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1898-wadesauce","name":"wadesauce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:46:52-07:00","id":566680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wadesauce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566645-roll-playing-totem-creation#post566645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is there a gift or Rite necessary for binding your totem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you have to be in the hisil, if not, would it be easier in terms hisil? </div> </div> </div>You don't need to be in the Hisil, but it will certainly be easier to find appropriate spirits there!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you have to hunt down the spirit and forcibly bind it as your totem, or do you negotiate with it? Is either route viable? </div> </div> </div>Both routes viable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do you determine what sort of spirit it's going to be? </div> </div> </div>Well, you ... choose? I mean, it's not random. A pack goes after a spirit that they feel appropriately reflects their pack or purpose, or the strengths they want to gain, etc.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:54:29-07:00","id":566691,"title":"","content":"Thanks.. I just need to figure out that binding part..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1898-wadesauce","name":"wadesauce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T11:25:23-07:00","id":566718,"title":"","content":"Think of it less as a binding, more of an agreement. You aren't trapping the spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T11:34:51-07:00","id":566730,"title":"","content":"Oh. So then forcing a spirit into a totem is more like, once it's hunted, then bested, it would become your totem out of respect for your dominance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1898-wadesauce","name":"wadesauce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T11:39:06-07:00","id":566732,"title":"","content":"You don't force it into a totem, a totem isn't an object, it's just a term for a spirit that has aligned itself with a pack. You could hunt it and best it, but that would probably only be important for a spirit that is about dominance or fighting.<br /> <br /> You could read the tribal origins. The Firstborn are tribal totems, and each has a story as for how they've been convinced to do so. If you have one of the older books on Lodges they tend to have interesting stories about how spirits agreed to patron lodges as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-24-2015, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T12:07:06-07:00","id":566765,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean force it into an objext, I meant force it into the roll of pact totem. . . But I see where your coming from. This information helped me a lot. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1898-wadesauce","name":"wadesauce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T12:24:32-07:00","id":566778,"title":"","content":"You *could* pin a spirit in a Shadowbind rite circle and offer to let it out only on the condition that it acquiesces to becoming your totem, but that's probably not a brilliant idea - a totem that resents the pack is not going to be the best ally ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T12:27:59-07:00","id":566804,"title":"","content":"Why would a spirit want to be a packs totem? As far as I can tell, the uratha actively hunt spirits, eat them for essence and not much else. It's the uratha sworn duty to keep the spirits in check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1898-wadesauce","name":"wadesauce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T12:32:27-07:00","id":566808,"title":"","content":"A spirit serving the role of a pack's totem is clearly exempt from that predation, and in fact pretty much gets a cult of the fiercest hunters this side of mortality working to feed them. It also helps open up the mortal world for them in a couple of ways. It can be a pretty sweet deal, actually. Not every spirit is going to want to serve the role of a totem, for their own reasons, but plenty can find it appealing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T12:52:16-07:00","id":566823,"title":"","content":"Well when you put it like that. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1898-wadesauce","name":"wadesauce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T14:01:10-07:00","id":566907,"title":"","content":"Totem spirits are also given a free pass by Uratha to be in the physical world. Werewolves can sense the totem bond - they may find other reasons to hunt a totem spirit, but it's not because it's on the wrong side of the Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T14:38:53-07:00","id":567021,"title":"","content":"Some packs maybe... the surest way to weaken a pack is to attack and discorporate/eliminate their totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T14:46:26-07:00","id":567032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wadesauce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566645-roll-playing-totem-creation?p=566804#post566804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the uratha sworn duty to keep the spirits in check.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. The parts that say this seem more like relics of first edition. They seem more about the hunt than being spirit police. The first tenet of the Oath of the Moon is, 'The Wolf Must Hunt.'<br /> <br /> As for why. Werewolves are effectively part spirit, part of them works with that side, so spirits have the same reasons to want to join a pack humans might. Protection, to get a lobbyist in the spirit courts, to have a potentially powerful attack squad, to keep essence coming that might otherwise die out, since a pack is resonant with whatever the totem is. Really, some of the same reasons werewolves might want a totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T09:10:21-07:00","id":568052,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Wolf Must Hunt... and Spirits are Prey. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T09:28:07-07:00","id":568068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566645-roll-playing-totem-creation?p=568052#post568052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Wolf Must Hunt... and Spirits are Prey. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits are one kind of prey among many, yes. But becoming a pack's Totem still comes with a lot of benefits, not the least of which is no longer being considered prey by the pack or its allies. Alongside that you've got easy access to a Locus, the veneration, protection, and obedience of a pack of deadly hunters, and a convenient means of crossing the Gauntlet. Like honestly it's a pretty sweet deal, as long as the spirit can find a pack whose interests align with theirs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:10:36-07:00","id":568110,"title":"","content":"All true... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}